     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I have an app that uploads a dataset that can be larger than 1mb. The app is on a our university shiny server</span><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">files less than 1mb have no problem. Files greater than 1mb give the following e<font color=\"#000000\">rror: &quot;<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:20px;text-align:center\">413 Request Entity Too Large&quot; </span></font> . More specifically a screenshot is attached for what it says. </span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">I have  had the option </span>base::options(shiny.maxRequestSize=100*1024^2)  there the whole time. </div><div><br></div><div>Any ideas?</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></span></div></div>"
